"Tracker:
https://example.atlassian.net

Map:
jira:example:TEST:map:TEST-470

Ticket:
jira:example:TEST:ticket:TEST-492 — Prepare a real pickup

Role:
task

Role guidance:
Implement only the selected task and verify its acceptance criteria. Report the implementation artifact and verification evidence.

Description:
PROBLEM
Pickup is missing.
ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
- Claim before creating a worktree.
- Return the T3 launch arguments.

Acceptance criteria:
- Claim before creating a worktree.
- Return the T3 launch arguments.

Required output:
- Report the work performed and link any resulting artifacts.
- Report acceptance evidence, unverified criteria, and remaining blockers.

Lane procedure:
1. Before any work, run \`bun <cli> lane attach --ticket jira:example:TEST:ticket:TEST-492 --json --state <state>\` from this worktree. If it refuses, report the refusal and stop. Its value.id is LANE below.
2. Implement and commit on this branch only. Do not push, open, edit or merge pull requests, and do not use GitHub write tools or credentials; Interlock pushes and opens the pull request.
3. When your checks pass at HEAD, run \`bun <cli> lane submit LANE --head SHA --gate GATE --evidence-url URL --json --state <state>\` with the full HEAD SHA, the check you ran, and a link to its result for that SHA. It pushes the branch and opens or updates this lane's one pull request.
4. Call link_pull_request with the returned value.artifact URL, then watch_pull_request on it. Link and watch no other pull request.
5. Run \`bun <cli> lane review LANE --json --state <state>\`. Then start one fresh delegate_task per review lens, in parallel, with role review and the exact target below. Brief each with the lens, the PR URL and the head SHA; each returns approved or changes_requested with findings.
   - correctness: target {"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"test-model","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}}
6. Record one verdict for that head: \`bun <cli> lane verdict LANE --head SHA --decision approved --state <state>\` only when every lens approved; otherwise --decision changes_requested --findings with every finding joined. On changes_requested, fix, commit and repeat from step 3 with the new head; the lane routes to attention at its review round limit.
7. Merge is not yours. When the watched pull request merges at the approved head, run \`bun <cli> lane complete --ticket jira:example:TEST:ticket:TEST-492 --json --state <state>\`, which verifies the merge and remote claim, moves the ticket to Done and leaves this worktree and branch intact. Repeat the same command after an interruption to recover the journaled completion. Then unwatch the pull request.
Interlock refusals are final for that step: report them instead of working around them.

Authorization and completion:
Apart from the Interlock lane commands above, this prompt does not grant authority to mutate tracker state, close tickets, or update maps. Follow the project/workflow instructions and explicit authorization for those actions. Passing acceptance checks alone does not authorize completion; all configured completion gates and required human approvals must also be satisfied."
,
      "modelSelection": {
        "harness": "codex",
        "instanceId": "codex",
        "model": "test-model",
        "options": {
          "reasoningEffort": "high",
        },
      },
      "runtimeMode": "full-access",
      "title": "TEST-492: Prepare a real pickup",
